{"metadata":{"category":"WorkspaceAssistant","title":"Giving the Agent Tools","role":"project","categoryPathComponent":"Table-of-Contents"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Giving-the-Agent-Tools"},"kind":"project","sections":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tool is a Swift function the model may decide to call. Write four of them, each a thin adapter over one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Workspace"},{"type":"text","text":" command."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"estimatedTimeInMinutes":15,"backgroundImage":"wa-agent.png","chapter":"The Agent","title":"Giving the Agent Tools","image":"wa-agent.png","kind":"hero","projectFiles":"WorkspaceAssistant.zip"},{"kind":"tasks","tasks":[{"title":"Write the Four Tools","stepsSection":[{"media":null,"type":"step","caption":[],"code":"wa-03-tools-01.swift","runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tools.swift"},{"type":"text","text":" and add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AddTaskTool"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Guide"},{"type":"text","text":" describes each argument to the model, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"category"},{"type":"text","text":" reuses the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Generable"},{"type":"text","text":" enum from the model layer."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"media":null,"type":"step","caption":[],"code":"wa-03-tools-02.swift","runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CompleteTaskTool"},{"type":"text","text":". The model passes the user’s own words, such as “unit tests”, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"completeTask"},{"type":"text","text":" turns them into one task. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":" is needed because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Workspace"},{"type":"text","text":" lives on the main actor."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"media":null,"type":"step","caption":[],"code":"wa-03-tools-03.swift","runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrioritizeTaskTool"},{"type":"text","text":". Same shape, different command. Notice how little is in each tool: all the logic lives in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Workspace"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"media":null,"type":"step","caption":[],"code":"wa-03-tools-04.swift","runtimePreview":null,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwitchLayoutTool"},{"type":"text","text":". Its argument is the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BoardLayout"},{"type":"text","text":" enum itself, so the model can only choose grid, list or board. Leave the comment at the end; it marks where you’ll add your own tool in the last tutorial."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"contentSection":[{"media":"wa-diagram-tool.png","mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every tool has three parts. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"description"},{"type":"text","text":" tell the model "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"when"}]},{"type":"text","text":" to use it. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Generable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arguments"},{"type":"text","text":" say "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"what"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the model must fill in. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"call(arguments:)"},{"type":"text","text":" runs your code and returns "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"what really happened"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add an "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent"}]},{"type":"text","text":" folder for the agent’s files."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"anchor":"Write-the-Four-Tools"}]},{"assessments":[{"type":"multiple-choice","title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Where should the logic for changing a task live?"}]}],"content":[],"choices":[{"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Then the user’s taps would need a second copy of the same logic."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inside each tool’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"call(arguments:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tools stay thin adapters, and the agent can never do anything the user couldn’t."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Workspace"},{"type":"text","text":", so taps and tools share it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instructions guide the model’s choices; the actual change must happen in Swift."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the model’s instructions."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"multiple-choice","title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What does the model use to decide which tool to call?"}]}],"content":[],"choices":[{"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"They are the contract the model reads, so write them as carefully as an API."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tool’s name, description and argument guides."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The model never sees your implementation."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift code inside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"call(arguments:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Order doesn’t tell the model what a tool does."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The order the tools are registered in."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"assessments","anchor":"Check-Your-Understanding"},{"title":"Talking to the Agent","kind":"callToAction","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LanguageModelSession"},{"type":"text","text":" with the tools, send it the user’s request, and show each tool call in a chat while the board changes behind it."}],"action":{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Talking-to-the-Agent","overridingTitle":"Get started","isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get started"}]},"featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/tutorials\/workspace-assistant\/giving-the-agent-tools"]}],"hierarchy":{"modules":[{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Modelling-the-Board","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Modelling-the-Board#Describe-a-Task"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Modelling-the-Board#Create-the-Workspace"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Modelling-the-Board#Let-the-Agent-Name-Tasks-in-Its-Own-Words"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Modelling-the-Board#Check-Your-Understanding"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Drawing-the-Board","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Drawing-the-Board#Draw-a-Task-Tile"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Drawing-the-Board#Lay-Out-the-Board"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Drawing-the-Board#Show-the-Board"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Drawing-the-Board#Check-Your-Understanding"}]}],"reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Table-of-Contents\/The-Board"},{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Giving-the-Agent-Tools","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Giving-the-Agent-Tools#Write-the-Four-Tools"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Giving-the-Agent-Tools#Check-Your-Understanding"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Talking-to-the-Agent","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Talking-to-the-Agent#Create-the-Session"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Talking-to-the-Agent#Run-the-Agentic-Loop"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Talking-to-the-Agent#Build-the-Chat"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Talking-to-the-Agent#Open-the-Agent-from-the-Board"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Talking-to-the-Agent#Check-Your-Understanding"}]}],"reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Table-of-Contents\/The-Agent"},{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Working-Alongside-the-Agent","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Working-Alongside-the-Agent#Add-Tasks-Yourself"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Working-Alongside-the-Agent#Press-and-Hold-a-Tile"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Working-Alongside-the-Agent#Keep-the-Demo-Working-on-Any-Mac"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Working-Alongside-the-Agent#Check-Your-Understanding"}]},{"reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Your-First-Tool","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Your-First-Tool#Add-the-Command"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Your-First-Tool#Write-and-Register-the-Tool"},{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Your-First-Tool#Give-the-User-the-Same-Power"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Your-First-Tool#Check-Your-Understanding"}]}],"reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Table-of-Contents\/Working-Together"}],"paths":[["doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Table-of-Contents","doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Table-of-Contents\/$volume","doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Table-of-Contents\/The-Agent"]],"reference":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Table-of-Contents"},"references":{"wa-03-tools-03.swift":{"content":["import FoundationModels","","\/\/ The agent's four tools.","\/\/","\/\/ A tool is a function the model may decide to call. You give it:","\/\/   • a name and a description  → how the model knows WHEN to use it","\/\/   • @Generable Arguments      → what the model must fill in (it can't invent other fields)","\/\/   • call(arguments:)          → your Swift code, which returns what really happened","\/\/","\/\/ Each tool here is a thin adapter over one Workspace command.","","struct AddTaskTool: Tool {","    let name = \"addTask\"","    let description = \"Adds a new task to the board.\"","    let workspace: Workspace","","    @Generable","    struct Arguments {","        @Guide(description: \"A short task title in Title Case, e.g. 'Review Pull Requests'\")","        var title: String","        var category: TaskCategory","        @Guide(description: \"True only if the user says the task is important, urgent or high priority\")","        var highPriority: Bool","    }","","    func call(arguments: Arguments) async throws -> String {","        await workspace.addTask(title: arguments.title, category: arguments.category, highPriority: arguments.highPriority, by: .agent)","    }","}","","struct CompleteTaskTool: Tool {","    let name = \"completeTask\"","    let description = \"Marks an existing task as done.\"","    let workspace: Workspace","","    @Generable","    struct Arguments {","        @Guide(description: \"The user's words for the task, e.g. 'unit tests'\")","        var task: String","    }","","    func call(arguments: Arguments) async throws -> String {","        await workspace.completeTask(arguments.task)","    }","}","","struct PrioritizeTaskTool: Tool {","    let name = \"prioritizeTask\"","    let description = \"Marks an existing task as high priority so it moves to the top.\"","    let workspace: Workspace","","    @Generable","    struct Arguments {","        @Guide(description: \"The user's words for the task, e.g. 'memory leak'\")","        var task: String","    }","","    func call(arguments: Arguments) async throws -> String {","        await workspace.prioritizeTask(arguments.task)","    }","}"],"fileType":"swift","syntax":"swift","identifier":"wa-03-tools-03.swift","fileName":"Tools.swift","highlights":[{"line":46},{"line":47},{"line":48},{"line":49},{"line":50},{"line":51},{"line":52},{"line":53},{"line":54},{"line":55},{"line":56},{"line":57},{"line":58},{"line":59},{"line":60},{"line":61}],"type":"file"},"doc://au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial/tutorials/Workspace-Assistant/Drawing-the-Board#Draw-a-Task-Tile":{"abstract":[{"text":"Draw the board in SwiftUI. Because the views only read ","type":"text"},{"code":"Workspace","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", every change, whether from a tap or from the agent, animates in by itself.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/workspace-assistant\/drawing-the-board#Draw-a-Task-Tile","identifier":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Drawing-the-Board#Draw-a-Task-Tile","title":"Draw a Task Tile","kind":"section","role":"pseudoSymbol","type":"section"},"doc://au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial/tutorials/Workspace-Assistant/Your-First-Tool":{"abstract":[{"text":"Teach the agent something new: removing high priority from a task. You’ll follow the same three steps every tool needs: a command, a tool, and registering it.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/tutorials\/workspace-assistant\/your-first-tool","estimatedTime":"15min","identifier":"doc:\/\/au.edu.uts.WorkspaceAssistant.tutorial\/tutorials\/Workspace-Assistant\/Your-First-Tool","title":"Your First Tool","kind":"project","role":"project","type":"topic"},"doc://a